# apply-drift-refile and its two shard drivers (b, c, which exec the parent's run.sh --group) share ONE declaration shape.
# apply-drift-refile drives apply.sh and its reconcile siblings, and copies the whole directory
# to build forced-failure copies. seed.sh and run.sh find it by a $0-rooted walk and read nothing else under the
# repo root. The preamble is sourced by run.sh.
